From b2a78ce00c286188075b1443fd2ea202dc3d4ffe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 17:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: meson: g12a-tohdmitx: reset via device_reset_optional
 under ACPI

The device is reset through an AML _RST method under ACPI, and only
the optional device_reset variant stops after evaluating it - the
non-optional variant falls through to an OF/lookup reset-control get
that cannot succeed without an of_node and fails the probe -ENOENT.
---
 sound/soc/meson/g12a-tohdmitx.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/meson/g12a-tohdmitx.c b/sound/soc/meson/g12a-tohdmitx.c
index d541ca4..7a19d09 100644
--- a/sound/soc/meson/g12a-tohdmitx.c
+++ b/sound/soc/meson/g12a-tohdmitx.c
@@ -249,7 +249,12 @@ static int g12a_tohdmitx_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	struct regmap *map;
 	int ret;
 
-	ret = device_reset(dev);
+	/*
+	 * Under ACPI the reset is an AML _RST method; only the optional
+	 * variant of device_reset() stops after evaluating it (the
+	 * non-optional variant still demands an OF/lookup reset control).
+	 */
+	ret = dev->of_node ? device_reset(dev) : device_reset_optional(dev);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
